.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH snip-theme-list 1  "snip 0.5.5" 
.SH NAME
snip\-theme\-list \- List available themes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsnip theme list\fR [\fB\-\-appearance\fR] [\fB\-\-library\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-simplified\-ui\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List available themes
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-appearance\fR \fI<APPEARANCE>\fR
Restrict to one appearance
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-library\fR \fI<LIBRARY>\fR
Library root. Falls back to SNIP_LIBRARY, ancestor discovery, then config
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Structured output mode for commands that return records
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
jsonl
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR
Color policy for terminal preview
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-simplified\-ui\fR[=\fI<BOOL>\fR]
Use square TUI bars without Powerline font glyphs for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
true
.IP \(bu 2
false
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
